From 27339d238891100dee264b56c127df86e08773f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Claude (Opus 5.5)" <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:55:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] SQLite3 driver: no stack overflow on long column names;
 NUL-safe text; BLOB values; bounded error messages

- FetchRow/SetRowCountVar built stem.column.n with sprintf into a fixed
  MAX_IDENTIFIER-sized stack buffer. SQLite column names are unbounded (an
  unaliased expression is named by its text): a long one aborted the whole
  interpreter (glibc: buffer overflow detected). Long names now use a heap
  buffer; an invalid Rexx name returns a normal error.
- Text values were measured with strlen(), truncating at the first NUL byte.
  Use sqlite3_column_bytes().
- BLOB values were always returned as the empty string. Return the bytes.
- Error messages: sprintf(tmp, ... %s identifier up to 255 bytes) into
  tmp[128] -> snprintf(tmp, sizeof(tmp), ...).
---
 general/rxsqlinc2.h |  20 ++++-----
 sqlite3/sqlite3.c   | 102 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--------------
 2 files changed, 79 insertions(+), 43 deletions(-)

